  "description": "A fixed 45-minute, two-problem mock format with checkpoints, a self-grading rubric for SDE-1/2/3, picking mocks from Tier A by company frequency, the debrief loop and a seven-day final-week plan built on revision cards.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Interview Hub</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">SDE-1 / SDE-2 / SDE-3</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Mock rounds and the last week before the interview</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Solving problems alone at your desk is training. A mock round is the match: a hard 45-minute clock, two unseen problems, talking out loud, no running the code until you have tested it in your head. This page gives you a fixed mock format, a self-grading rubric for each level, a way to pick mocks from the Tier A problems your target company asks most, and a seven-day plan for the final week built on your revision cards.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-start-here\">How coding rounds work</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-testing-your-code\">Testing your code in the interview</a> and <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-revision-system\">The revision system</a>. <b>Company detail:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-amazon\">Amazon</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-google\">Google</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-meta\">Meta</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-microsoft\">Microsoft</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
